# Documentation Style

Write documentation for future maintainers.

Be factual.

Avoid marketing language.

Prefer concise explanations.

Update version numbers where appropriate.

Preserve document structure.

Never delete historical information.

Mark deprecated content rather than silently removing it.

Maintain consistent terminology.

Use headings consistently.

Keep markdown clean.